  <front>
    <title>IANA Registries for LSP Ping Code Points</title>
    <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="7537" stream="IETF"/>
    <date year="2015" month="May"/>
    <abstract pn="section-abstract">
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">RFCs 4379 and 6424 created name spaces for Multi-Protocol Label
Switching (MPLS) Label Switched Path (LSP) Ping.  However, those RFCs
did not create the corresponding IANA registries for Downstream
Mapping object Flags (DS Flags), Multipath Types, Pad TLVs, and
Interface and Label Stack Address Types.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-2">There is now a need to make further code point allocations from these
name spaces.  This document updates RFCs 4379 and 6424 in that it
creates IANA registries for that purpose.</t>
    </abstract>
